{
  "abstract": "Over half of the known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. We invert this elimination by parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$, where the regular fifths become linear in the trace $S_{ab}$ and all three remaining conditions complete the square in $S_{ab}$. Vanishing of their discriminants cuts out two families of sextuple and $19/21$ septuple surfaces: the Branch-1 surface $E_{Br1}$ and the twin-fifth surfaces $E_{F1}, E_{F3}$. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and a new rational almost septuple $S_7^{(20/21)}$ of relation type $(5,2)$. Factoring the four-variable regular relation on the fifths defines $S_{4,2}$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. In $(r,\\mu,z)$ and Lorentz $(r,u,v,\\theta)$ coordinates, we establish the One-$R_5$ Dual Brahmagupta blow-up $P_{blowup}=0$ and Two-Conic surface $P_{surf}=0$ covering $N_{core}=0$ ($4:1$), classify sub-regular and collision curves (including the genus-five slice $F_{12}=0$ and a $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{133})$ almost septuple), and prove a $2$-adic lock on $E_B$ and rank-zero descent on $E_{16}$. Finally, we establish $3$-torsion Master Syzygies closing $C_{triad}$ and $H=1/3$, paired/antipodal source closures, the Monomial Fifth Law, and the Bi-Euler towers $U_{4N+3}^{biEuler}$ on the symplectic Euler plane $V_{Euler}$ in a free rank-three $\\mathbb{Z}[r]$-module $M_3$ with a genus-four coincidence curve $C_{coinc,r}$. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 23 implements all five referee recommendations from the Version 22 acceptance report (restricting the t-odd free rank-3 Z[r]-module statement M_3 = Z[r]*a + Z[r]*b + Z[r]*r_{a,d_-} to the 9 entries, the t-odd roots R_{c,a}, R_{c,g}, R_{a,g}, and the 10 t-odd bases X_1, tilde{X}_1, X_2, X_4, tilde{X}_4, X_5, X_6, X_{11}, X_{12}, X_{13}, while placing the t-even base X_3 = (2*r^2-1)^2*r + (4*r^2-1)*b*r_{a,d_-} in the complementary t-even free rank-2 module N_2^{even} = Z[r]*r + Z[r]*(b*r_{a,d_-}); correcting the paired sign exponent to (1 -/+ 1)/2 in the compressed -/+ b diagonal formulas for 1+c*f_{c,-} and 1+g_{Euler,+}*tilde{g}_{Euler,+}; describing iota_{A,C}(t,Y)=(C/(A*t), C*Y/(A*t^2)) as the reciprocal involution infty_+ (-) P with iota_{A,C}^*(dt/Y) = -dt/Y and certifying infinite order of P_1(r) on E_I(r^2), E_II(r^2) via strict r-degree growth deg_r(t([n]P_1)) = 2, 12, 26 and 2, 10, 22 for n=1,2,3; basing the squareness of Q_I, Q_II on C_{coinc,r} directly on the explicit polynomial division identities and clarifying that [26] proves general type unconditionally; and clarifying that t_{III}(r) = -t_{sec}(r) from Item 22 and that the 9 6/6 sub-quadruples of S_6^{refl}(r) split R_5=0 over Q(r) into 3 zero branches on R_4 plus 15 distinct 18/21 septuple families certified at r=2) and adds Theorem 20(60)-(62) (Item 26 in THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md, verified in exp67): (1) the (E_1, E_2, E_3) basis (E_1*E_2 = -1/r^2, E_1*E_3 + E_2*E_3 = 4*(r^2-1)), the Universal Lagrange 2x2 Minor Identity, and the Symplectic Euler Plane V_{Euler} = {(p_+, p_-, s) : p_+ + p_- = 2*r^2*s} = Q(r)*e_1 + Q(r)*e_2 where 1 + u(w_1)*u(w_2) = R(w_1,w_2)^2 + 1 - (xi_1*eta_2 - eta_1*xi_2)^2; (2) the Four Universal Master Laws on V_{Euler} showing 1+d_-*u(xi,eta) and 1+b*u(xi,eta) share the shift 1 - Q(xi,eta) (Q(xi,eta) = xi^2 + 2*(2*r^2-1)*xi*eta + eta^2); and (3) the universal closed-form osculating section t_{b,(xi,eta)}(r) making 1+b*u(xi,eta)=square and the Chebyshev (4N+3)-element tower U_{4N+3}^{bi-Euler}(r,t) in M_3 with 12N+1 automatic squares (13/21, 25/55, 37/105 at N=1,2,3) and 8N^2-2N+2 r-only shifts, together with U_{13}^{bi-Euler}(r,t) (29/78 squares, 49 r-only shifts) and the genus-0 conic reduction 1+d_-*g_0 = (2*r^2*t)^2 - (4*r^2-1).",
